<title>CHINA: China Jan-Sept steel output up 4.16 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>China Jan-Sept steel output up 4.16 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's steel output hit 74.0 million tonnes in January to September, a rise of 4.16 percent from the same period last year, the Xinhua news agency said on Monday.</p>
<p>Output of rolled steel was up 6.85 percent during the period to 63.16 million tonnes while production of ferro-alloy increased by 7.39 percent to 2.62 million tonnes, Xinhua said.</p>
<p>Production of pig iron fell to 78.5 million tonnes and iron ore output slipped to 181.46 million tonnes, both drops of 2.58 percent, it said.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
</text>
